{
  "rationale": "The model separates sensing from motion capability and uses small deterministic specifications to bind each sensed condition to exactly one safe action. Clear conditions strongly favor forward progress via move_forward and occasional brief random_walk, while obstacle conditions force one-shot recovery actions only. Front obstacles trigger a brief backward escape before returning quickly to forward exploration when path_clear appears. Left/right obstacles use consistent directed turns away from the blocked side. full_rotate is included in the plant as an available capability but intentionally left unused by the specifications so it remains a last-resort option outside the nominal supervisor.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use one sensor plant and one motion-capability plant.",
    "Use perception-to-action specifications with one enabled controllable per decision state.",
    "Bias clear operation toward move_forward, with a small alternation spec to occasionally permit random_walk.",
    "Use obstacle-specific recovery states: front -> move_backward, left -> rotate_clockwise, right -> rotate_counterclockwise.",
    "Make recovery actions one-shot and return to exploration immediately on path_clear.",
    "In action states, self-loop on path_clear and only obstacle events preempt for safety."
  ],
